Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add test_gdn_replay.py: GDN replay kernel checks and
 history/replay A/B

Standalone GPU-owner script (not collected by pytest; resolves the models
relative to the checkout's parent directory).
- --state-check-only [--state-channelwise]: compares the replay commit
  (eager and batched) against the history path's state for every accepted
  length, scalar and channelwise decay, bsz 1 and 2, without loading models.
- Model A/B: mode 0 (history), mode 1 (replay, BC-graph verify, batched
  commit) and optionally mode 2 (--eager-replay), each in a fresh child, with
  greedy output compared token for token. Mode 1 checks that every GDN
  layer's captured replay-verify graph actually launched; --alternating-cache
  verifies on two caches with records pending in both; --graph-reinst N runs
  every child with EXL3_GRAPH_REINST=N.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
